Lab: Manage Application Updates
Objective
•	Update two live applications to use specific image versions rather than floating tags.
•	Configure image triggers so OpenShift automatically rolls out updates when image stream tags change.
________________________________________
1. Prepare Lab Environment
lab start updates-review
•	Sets up updates-review project.
•	Deploys two apps: app1 and app2.
•	Prepares resources.txt with image details.
Login and set project:
oc login -u developer -p developer https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
oc project updates-review
________________________________________
2. Update app1 Deployment to Use a Static Image Tag
•	Current deployment uses floating latest tag.
Check deployment:
oc get deployment/app1 -o wide
Update image to static tag 1-222:
oc set image deployment/app1 \
  php-ssl=registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/redhattraining/php-ssl:1-222
Verify:
oc get deployment/app1 -o wide
•	app1 now uses php-ssl:1-222.
________________________________________
3. Configure app2 Deployment for Image Trigger
•	app2 uses php-ssl:1 tag (alias for 1-222).
•	Enable automatic rollout whenever php-ssl:1 changes.
Retrieve container name:
oc get deployment/app2 -o wide
Add image trigger:
oc set triggers deployment/app2 \
  --from-image php-ssl:1 --containers php-ssl
Verify triggers:
oc set triggers deployment/app2
Output shows image php-ssl:1 (php-ssl) with AUTO = true.
________________________________________
4. Deploy New Image Version for app2
•	New tested image: php-ssl:1-234.
Create new image stream tag:
oc create istag php-ssl:1-234 \
  --from-image registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/redhattraining/php-ssl:1-234
Move alias php-ssl:1 to point to the new tag:
oc tag --alias php-ssl:1-234 php-ssl:1
Verify app2 rollout:
oc describe deployment/app2
•	Old replica set scales down.
•	New replica set scales up automatically.
________________________________________
5. Finish Lab
Grade and clean up:
lab grade updates-review
lab finish updates-review
________________________________________
Key Concepts
1.	Static image tags prevent accidental redeployment of untested images.
2.	Image triggers enable automatic rolling updates when image stream tags change.
3.	Aliases allow floating tags (like php-ssl:1) to point to specific versioned tags (like 1-222 or 1-234) safely.
4.	Rolling update workflow:
o	Old pods coexist with new pods during rollout.
o	Replica sets scale up/down automatically.
5.	Reproducible deployments: SHA IDs or static tags ensure consistent images are used.

